Based on my exploration of the codebase, I understand the Monte Carlo integration pattern. The mean value method estimates the integral as (b-a) times the average of function values at random sample points.

```cpp
    double sum = 0.0;
    double range = b - a;

    for (int i = 0; i < n_points; i++) {
        // Generate uniform random number in [0,1) using LCG
        seed = (1103515245 * seed + 12345) % 2147483648;
        double u = static_cast<double>(seed) / 2147483648.0;

        // Transform to [a,b] range
        double x = a + u * range;

        // Accumulate function values
        sum += f(x);
    }

    // Mean value theorem: integral ≈ (b-a) * average of f values
    return range * sum / n_points;
```

